  {
   "index": 13,
   "tag": "p×5",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 832,
   "text": "neverthrow is faster than mine. In that test its errors are bare objects with no name and no message, and mine are real instanceof Error objects with both, so I'm happy to leave the gap. Plain try/catch wins too when nothing fails at all: 195 ns vs my 203.\nThe large gap is on the failure path, and it comes from error construction. Creating an Error subclass took 1,978 ns. An errval error took 25 n",
